  "statement": "Read a list of integers and print the sum of the even ones and the sum of the odd ones.\n\nInput: the first line holds n (0 <= n <= 1000). The second line holds n integers a_1 .. a_n (-10^6 <= a_i <= 10^6), separated by spaces. When n is 0 the second line is empty.\nOutput: one line \"E O\" where E is the sum of the even numbers and O the sum of the odd numbers. A negative number is even or odd like its absolute value (-3 is odd, -4 is even, 0 is even). An empty sum is 0.\n\nExample\nInput:\n5\n1 2 3 4 -5\nOutput:\n6 -1\n(even: 2+4 = 6, odd: 1+3-5 = -1)",
  "starter_code": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    cin >> n;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        int x;\n        cin >> x;\n        // Your code here\n    }\n    // Print the even sum and the odd sum\n}\n",
